            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0719" n="637" xml:id="pg637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3307: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-01T14:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                                1925—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>135. Referring to the Legation’s No. 134, August 29, 5 p.m. Martial law declared
                    in Managua yesterday. Railroad communication resumed, otherwise situation
                    remains unchanged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
